---
import PolicyLayout from '~/layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/config/site';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using Formatoza's free in-browser file converters: acceptable use, your content, no warranty and limitation of liability."
  path="/terms/"
  h1="Terms of service"
  lead={`By using ${SITE.name}, you agree to these terms. They are written to be short and readable.`}
  updated="September 25, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} provides free file-conversion tools that run in your web browser. We may add, change
    or remove tools at any time. The service is provided free of charge and supported by
    advertising.
  </p>
  <h2>2. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep all rights to the files you convert. Because conversion happens on your device, we do
    not receive, store or have access to your files. You are responsible for having the right to
    convert and use the files you process, including any copyright, licence or confidentiality
    obligations that apply to them.
  </p>
  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the service for anything unlawful, or to infringe others' rights;</li>
    <li>
      attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the website or its infrastructure;
    </li>
    <li>
      scrape, frame or republish the site's content or code in a way that misrepresents its origin;
    </li>
    <li>
      interfere with the advertising that funds the service through fraudulent clicks or
      impressions.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>4. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The converters are provided “as is” and “as available”. We work hard to make them accurate and
    document their known limitations on each page, but we do not guarantee that any conversion is
    complete, error-free or suitable for a particular purpose. Always keep your original files and
    check important results before relying on them.
  </p>
  <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} and its operators are not liable for any
    indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for any loss of data, arising from your use of
    the service. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>
  <h2>6. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses third-party services for hosting and advertising, and links to external websites.
    We are not responsible for their content or practices; their own terms and policies apply.
  </p>
  <h2>7. Open-source software</h2>
  <p>
    Some converters include open-source libraries such as PDF.js, pdf-lib, Mammoth, Papa Parse,
    fast-xml-parser, js-yaml, marked, Turndown, UTIF, libheif (via heic-to) and libwebp (via
    jSquash), each used under its own licence.
  </p>
  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms; the date above shows the latest version. Continued use after changes
    means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>
  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
